[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hi everyone, welcome back to 51 Drones. What I\'d like to show you today are a couple of the intelligent flight features on the anti-gravity A1 360 camera drone. I\'m going to show you the sky path, which is basically way points. So that\'s where you can fly the drone to'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'certain positions, lock it in that position, and then make a, you know, like a route for it to follow, and then run it automatically, and it\'ll record everything for you, and then you can go in after the fact and edit the footage. Uh, I\'m also going to show you the deep'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'track mode, which is basically focus tracking or active tracking as most of you know. And I\'m just going to do a simple tutorial on that. I\'m going to show you how to set it up, how to do it, how to change directions and things like'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that. So, I\'m going to do first with walking and then I\'m going to show you some uh tests that I did with my vehicle, the deep tracking on the vehicle. Spoiler alert, I\'m going to tell you it needs some work. It really does. As far as walking, it\'s really'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'good. Like, it it works wonderfully. like I think it might work better than any other drone I\'ve ever flown when it comes to tracking a walking person, but a vehicle it\'s one of the worst. So'

[01:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hopefully they hopefully they fix that. Hopefully they bring it together because uh well you\'ll see here in just a second, but I\'ll show you. So and then it\'s also a good day to test out how this thing can fly in windy conditions'

[01:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because it\'s about 30 mph winds today. I\'m hiding behind my pickup right now, but we\'re going to venture out into the wind and we\'re going to see how this thing tracks in windy conditions. So, all right. So, let\'s get the drone up'

[01:25] [scene:talk]
